// Title: Scheduled Task Executing Encoded Payload from Registry
// ID: c4eeeeae-89f4-43a7-8b48-8d1bdfa66c78
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: pH-T (Nextron Systems), @Kostastsale, TheDFIRReport, X__Junior (Nextron Systems), Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-02-12
// Tags: attack.privilege-escalation, attack.execution, attack.persistence, attack.t1053.005, attack.t1059.001
// Description: Detects the creation of a schtask that potentially executes a base64 encoded payload stored in the Windows Registry using PowerShell.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((src.process.cmdline containsCIS "/Create") AND ((src.process.cmdline containsCIS "FromBase64String" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS "encodedcommand")) AND ((src.process.cmdline containsCIS "Get-ItemProperty" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS " gp ")) AND ((src.process.cmdline containsCIS "HKCU:" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS "HKLM:" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS "registry::" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS "HKEY_")) AND ((src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\schtasks.exe") OR (OriginalFileName = "schtasks.exe")))
